<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humban-haltash III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">captured 640 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humban-haltash III was the last known king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> destroyed Susa in 646 BCE, he was captured in 640 BCE and paraded as a prisoner. His fall marks the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> as an independent power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/humban-haltash-iii.jpg" alt="Humban-haltash III" width="302" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anthony Huan · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Ummanaldash_captured_by_the_Assyrians.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
